Author: Christian Richardson <christianrichardson.finance@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 09:20:41 2026 -0400

    Add email/password auth with server-side sessions, CSRF check and login rate limits

    - users and sessions tables (citext email, hashed session tokens)
    - Signup, login, logout and me endpoints, validated with shared zod schemas
    - argon2id password hashing; the same 401 for a wrong password and an
      unknown email, with timing equalized by a dummy hash check
    - Sessions: random 256-bit token in an httpOnly SameSite=Lax cookie, only
      its SHA-256 stored; sliding expiry; a new session on every login, and
      the browser's previous one revoked
    - Global SessionGuard (opt out with @Public(), fails closed for non-HTTP
      transports) and @CurrentActor()
    - Global CSRF guard: Origin, else Referer, must match APP_BASE_URL;
      cookie-authenticated requests with neither are rejected
    - Login rate limits per IP and per email (in memory), signup per IP
    - New env: SESSION_TTL_DAYS, COOKIE_SECURE, TRUST_PROXY_HOPS, RATE_LIMIT_LOGIN_*
    - Module folders: types in <folder>.types.ts, services in *.service.ts,
      auth split into sessions/, csrf/ and passwords/
    - CLAUDE.md with the codebase conventions; rate-limiting improvements
      (Redis with TTLs) noted in ENHANCEMENTS.md
    - Unit and e2e tests for all of the above

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

